WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:09.799
A lazy afternoon in a Hutong - one
of Beijing's traditional residential alleys

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:11.120
in the heart of the city.

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:13.880
This is Backstreet Beijing.

00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:17.789
It smells of fresh vegetables, seafood and
pastry.

00:00:17.789 --> 00:00:21.310
People here have turned their houses into
small shops and eateries.

00:00:21.310 --> 00:00:27.380
For years, these restaurants and kiosks have attracted not only locals but also an international crowd.

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:32.380
But recently, the residents have received unwelcome guests.

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:38.000
Notices like these have spelled the end of
busy shopping and eating alleys.

00:00:38.019 --> 00:00:42.940
The government is taking action against building work
that has been done without a proper licence.

00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:46.980
And that’s hitting those little shops and
restaurants in the alleys.

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:54.420
Traditionally these houses are open onto the
courtyard and are walled towards the streets.

00:00:54.429 --> 00:01:00.449
New outward doors and windows are unlicensed -  illegal.

00:01:00.449 --> 00:01:03.079
The city government sent workers to brick
them.

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:05.540
You need to be quick if you want to use them.

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:14.500
“The shop has helped us to make some money,
to improve our lives.

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:17.710
So of course we don’t like this
decision.

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:18.960
But what can we do?

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:22.460
If the government says so, we have to obey
- don’t we?”

00:01:27.009 --> 00:01:30.140
Authorities have declined to comment on this
issue.

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:33.060
More than one thousand alleys are under threat.

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:36.120
Shop owners there stand to lose their livelihoods.

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:40.259
“For me it’s tough.

00:01:40.259 --> 00:01:42.310
Im selling almost nothing recently.

00:01:42.310 --> 00:01:47.040
I think I have no other choice than to go back
to my home province.”

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:55.900
For the moment, she and her neighbors do their best 
to keep their shops open.

00:01:55.900 --> 00:02:01.560
And finding creative ways to avoid
standing on a stool by a tiny window all day.

